  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.50) as it often signals downward pressure.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility after sharp spikes; model tends to overreact and overshoot in the short term.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates >10% from recent 5-day average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "For horizon >15 days, reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if sentiment remains neutral or positive, to avoid overconfidence.",
    "If sentiment turns positive (e.g., 0.50) after a downtrend, increase forecast slope gradually to avoid sudden rebounds.",
    "Correct for lag: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, delay correction by 1-2 days to account for market inertia."
  ]
